                "senderName": "NWS Albuquerque NM",
                "headline": "Flash Flood Warning issued September 25 at 2:56PM MDT until September 25 at 4:30PM MDT by NWS Albuquerque NM",
                "description": "At 256 PM MDT, Doppler radar indicated the heaviest rainfall has\nended across the warned area. Up to 1.25 inches of rain have fallen\nin the area between Casa Blanca Road, Marmon Ranch Road, and Sunset\nRoad east of Acoma Pueblo and south of Laguna Pueblo. Additional\nrainfall amounts up to 0.50 inches are possible with the next batch\nof showers and thunderstorms. Flash flooding is ongoing or expected\nto begin shortly.\n\nHAZARD...Life threatening flash flooding. Thunderstorms producing\nflash flooding.\n\nSOURCE...Radar indicated.\n\nIMPACT...Life threatening flash flooding of creeks and streams, urban\nareas, highways, streets and underpasses.\n\nSome locations that will experience flash flooding include...\nLaguna Pueblo, New Laguna, Mesita, Acoma Pueblo, Paraje, Seama and\nAcomita.\n\nThis includes Interstate 40 between Mile Markers 106 and 122.",
